<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75885" body-key="">
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μήν,</span></b> 
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not however</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1068
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὴν οὐδέ</span>
			<i>nor on the other hand</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				82
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.5
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὴν . . γε</span> after a neg., <i>no
				nor even yet</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀφροδίτης γὰρ οὔ μοι φαίνεται, οὐ
					μὴν Χαρίτων γε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					41
				</span></i>
			: without a preceding neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὴν
				ἐρῶ γ᾽ ὡς</span> . . <i>I cannot, it is true</i>, say .
			. , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				53
			</span></i>; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μάν</span>
			.</div>
	</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
